<title>USA: Singapore to upgrade Boeing tankers for $500 mln.</title>
<headline>Singapore to upgrade Boeing tankers for $500 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense Department announced that Singapore plans to purchase $500 million in logistics support to upgrade four Boeing Co KC-135A military tanker aircraft.</p>
<p>Boeing and CFM International of Cincinnati, Ohio, would be the chief contractors on the work to upgrade the planes, which were earlier sold to Singapore. The $500 million would be paid by Singapore to upgrade the KC-135A aircraft to more advanced &quot;R&quot; model configuration, the Pentagon said.</p>
</text>
